/*
| Workplans, lanes and the broker (client 1.11.0; SECTIONS 29 to 33,
| privacy rule 3a). Each is a mirror of the server's (hive.workplans,
| hive.broker, the Broker enums, BrokerMessage::PARAM_KEYS); a test holds
| each pair together. The policy's workplans and broker blocks override
| the numbers where they name one, bounded whatever they say.
|
|   PLAN_FILE_GLOBS     the plan files rule 3a lets mark-dirty note and the
|                       detached plan-file run read, relative to the
|                       workspace root or a tracked repository, never in
|                       velu-hive (hive.workplans.plan_globs)
|   PLAN_FILE_EXCEPT    base names never read among them: a design doc, a
|                       README, an index (hive.workplans.plan_except)
|   PLAN_DOC_MAX        the largest document ever read or sent, whole or not
|                       at all: 2 MiB, the server's doc_max_bytes. The
|                       policy's workplans.doc_max_bytes sets the limit,
|                       held to 1 KB to this (hive_plan_doc_max())
|   PLAN_DOC_FALLBACK   the limit while the cache names none (no policy yet,
|                       a server older than 1.11.0's): 64 KB, what every
|                       client up to 1.21.2 sent, so a machine that has not
|                       heard the owners' value never sends more than that
|   PLAN_FILE_DEBOUNCE  seconds a written plan file waits for its run, per file
|   PLAN_SYNC_EVERY     seconds between two syncs of one workspace's
|                       PROGRESS.md files (the policy's
|                       workplans.sync_every_minutes)
|   PLAN_SYNC_ROOT      the folder the sync lists on the remote default branch
|   PLAN_PUSHED_RECHECK seconds between two checks, after a Bash call, of
|                       whether a captured plan reached its upstream
|   PLAN_WANTS_MAX      plan documents one sync run sends because Hive asked
|   PLAN_SYNC_COST_PER_MINUTE, PLAN_SYNC_CAPTURE_COST   what the token may
|                       spend a minute and what one capture of a plan costs
|                       it (hive.rate_limits.cost_per_minute and
|                       hive.workplans.publish_cost; held to them by
|                       ClientWorkplanContractTest): the client's own,
|                       for a policy that does not serve them -- from
|                       Hive 2.10.10 the policy's workplans block names
|                       both, and the sync takes those
|                       (hive_plan_sync_send_max())
|   PLAN_SYNC_MINUTE_SHARE   a sync run spends at most 1/this of that minute
|                       (hive_plan_sync_send_max(): 4 captures, 20 of 120).
|                       velu-workspace holds about 70 PROGRESS.md, and ten
|                       captures back to back drew a 429 that held the whole
|                       machine (hunt 7, H2). The rest go at the next run
|   PLAN_UPLOAD_STEP, PLAN_UPLOAD_BASE, PLAN_UPLOAD_MAX   the window a plan
|                       document over one step (256 KB) gets on a detached
|                       path: BASE seconds and one more per started step, at
|                       most MAX (hive_plan_upload_window(); HIVE_TIMEOUTS'
|                       plan-upload). A smaller one keeps the progress pair
|
|   AUTONOMY_VALUES, GATE_MODES   the broker's switches (policy broker.*)
|   BROKER_KINDS, BROKER_CODES, BROKER_SIDES, BROKER_UNTIL, BROKER_RULES,
|   BROKER_SUBJECTS, BROKER_CHOICES, BROKER_VERBS   the closed sets a broker
|                       block is read against (hive_broker_block()); anything
|                       else is dropped and counted, never shown
|   BROKER_NEXT_ARGS    the args each HIVE NEXT verb may carry, with their
|                       grammar (NextVerb::args())
|   BROKER_PARAM_KEYS   the only keys a message's params may hold, with their
|                       grammar (BrokerMessage::PARAM_KEYS)
|   BROKER_WATCH_SECONDS the idle watcher's window (policy broker.watch_seconds)
|   BROKER_WAKES_PER_HOUR exit-2 wakes a session gets an hour (policy
|                       broker.wakes_per_hour)
|   BROKER_REPEAT       seconds before an action still open is said again
|   BROKER_URGENT_WITHIN seconds to a request's deadline that make it urgent
|   BROKER_INBOX_WAIT_MAX the longest `progress inbox --wait`
|   BROKER_MESSAGES_MAX, BROKER_RULINGS_MAX   items read from one block
|   BROKER_TEXT_MAX     characters of Hive's sentence kept
|   BROKER_SAID_MAX     message ids broker-said.json keeps
|   BROKER_GATE_SAMPLES_MAX  gate samples one heartbeat sends
|   LANE_LEASE_BUDGET   seconds the lease may take before a lane task starts
|                       (the 3 s write budget); no answer is "unconfirmed"
|   AUTOPILOT_TAKES_PER_DAY  takes one session's autopilot makes a day
|   LANES_SESSION_KEEP  lanes.json forgets a session not seen this long
|   OVERRIDE_KEEP       lanes.json forgets an override this long after it
|   ACTIVITY_TOOL_KINDS what kind of work each tool's call is, for the live
|                       activity (section 2.8c; the server's ToolKind, whose
|                       values are this map's, SHELL_KINDS and `other`, for
|                       any tool not in it). Counted by the tool's name,
|                       never by what it was called with
|   ACTIVITY_SHELL_KINDS what a shell command is counted as when
|                       hive_activity_shell_kind() can tell what it ran
|                       (section 2.8d, rule 1b; ToolKind::shellKinds()):
|                       committing, pushing, a pull request, a review, a
|                       test run, a build. Any other is `shell`
|   ACTIVITY_DIRTY_KINDS the kinds whose calls can change files: mark-dirty
|                       marks a repository dirty only for these
|                       (ToolKind::changesFiles()). It decides by the tool's
|                       kind, before a command is read, so every shell
|                       command marks, whatever it ran
|   ACTIVITY_SEND_EVERY the longest a working session's counts wait for a
|                       request of their own, in seconds: they ride any
|                       request the flush makes anyway before that (the
|                       policy's activity.send_seconds, held to 10 to 120;
|                       hive.agents.activity_send_seconds)
|   ACTIVITY_NEWS_AFTER seconds after the last send at which news goes on a
|                       request of its own: a kind of work no report named
|                       lately, a sub-agent starting or finishing (the
|                       policy's activity.news_seconds: 0, never, else held
|                       to 5 to 60; hive.agents.activity_news_seconds)
|   ACTIVITY_NEWS_MEMORY seconds a kind stays known in a repository after a
|                       report named it there; named again later, it is news
|   ACTIVITY_NEWS_PER_MINUTE the most sends of news alone in any 60 seconds
|   ACTIVITY_SUBAGENTS_MAX the most sub-agents one send carries in
|                       `activity.agents`, the rest counted in `agents_more`
|                       (hive.agents.max_subagents_per_send)
|
|   The grammars every typed field is checked against before it reaches a
|   command line (SECTION 29): a workplan key, a ULID, a path hash, a git
|   sha, a repository name (TakeBacklogItemRequest::REPO_PATTERN), a lane
|   letter, a worktree name (WorkSettings: .worktrees/ and one name), and a
|   provisional ruling's token (v1.<payload>.<HMAC-SHA256>, base64url). And
|   the two a send checks before it carries them (section 2.8d): a
|   sub-agent's name (SubagentReport::TYPE_PATTERN) and the session's model
|   (AgentActivityReport::MODEL_PATTERN).
|
|   Since 1.12.0, a developer's label for a session
|   (SessionLabels::PATTERN, held together by ClientWorkplanContractTest):
|   lower-case letters, digits and dashes, 1 to 24, the first a letter or a
|   digit, so it is never read as an option. A label is data, never an
|   instruction: checked here before it is sent, and wherever one comes
|   back. And a session's handle, the first 12 hex of its digest, which
|   names a session nobody labelled.
*/
